      <div type="clause" n="76.1a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 76.1a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1a" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>Ac þære cægean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.24"/> heo sceal weardian, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is hyre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.25"/> hordern ⁊ hyre cyste ⁊ hyre tege<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1-4"/>: gif hit under þyssa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.2-3"/> ænigu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gebroht byð, þonne byð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.3-2"/> heo scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>Ac ðara cægan heo sceal weardian, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is hire heddernes cæge ⁊ hyre cyste cæge [⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1-2"/> hire tægan]: gyf hit under ðyssa ænigum gebroht byð, ðone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.2"/> bið heo scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76.1a" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>Ac þære cægen heo sceal weardian, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is hire hordern ⁊ hire cyste ⁊ hyre tyge: gif hit under þisse ænigu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gebroht byð, þonne bið hyo scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.1a" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Sed suum hórdern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.20"/> (quod dicere possumus dispensam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.21"/>) et cistam suam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1-3"/> et téage<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.2-2"/> (id est scrinium suum) debet ipsa custodire: si sub aliquo istorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.3"/> inueniatur, tunc ipsa quoque culpabilis habeatur.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.1a" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Has uero claues mulier debet sub cura sua custodire, scilicet dispensę<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1-5"/> suę et arcę et scrinii sui; sub his itaque clauibus si inuentum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.2-4"/> non fuerit, mulier sine culpa erit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.3-3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76.1a" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>[76, 1<hi rend="italic">a</hi>] He autem sere sunt, quas marita obseruare debet: sera dispense et ciste et scrinii; quodsi sub aliqua harum locatum sit, non iudicetur innocens.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="76.1a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="214" ed="#robertson"/>Ac ðara cægan heo sceal weardian, þæt is hire heddernes cæge<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1a.robnote.fn.1"/> ⁊ hyre cyste cæge<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76-1a.robnote.fn.2"/> [⁊ hire tægan]<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_76-1a.robnote.fn.3"/>; gyf hit under ðyssa ænigum gebroht byð, ðone<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_76-1a.robnote.fn.4"/> bið heo scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="294" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Ac þære cægean heo sceal weardian: þæt is hyre hordern and hyre cyste and hyre tege; gif hit under þyssa ænigum gebroht byð, þonne byð heo scyldig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Dagegen auf folgende (-den?<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.1"/>) Schlüssel muss sie Acht geben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.2"/>, nämlich ihre Vorrathskammer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.3"/> (-Schlüssel <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) und ihre Kiste und ihren Schrein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.4"/> [beaufsichtigen]: wenn jenes unter deren eines gebracht worden ist, dann ist sie schuldig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.5"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">On the other hand, she must keep watch over the following key (keys?), namely [look after] her storeroom (storeroom key, B) and her chest and her casket: if it has been brought under any one of these, then she is guilty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="215" ed="#robertson"/>But it is her duty to guard the keys of the following—her storeroom and her chest and her cupboard<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76-1a.robnote.n.1"/>. If the goods have been put in any of these, she shall be held guilty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="473" ed="#whitelock"/>But she must look after the keys of the following: namely her storeroom, her chest and her coffer; if it is brought inside any of these, she is then guilty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="295" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And these are the keys for which she shall be responsible: her storeroom, her chest, and her cupboard; if the goods have been placed in any of these, she shall be considered guilty.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 363, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">hordern: heddernes cæge B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">cyste: cyste cæge B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þonne: þone B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hee sunt a. se. <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hee sunt a. se. Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sera <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sera added by Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. am Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in the margin in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 25</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">see above 25</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">horden <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">horden T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-sa <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-sa T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">teáge <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>; scirc <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">teáge Hk; scirc K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iust. <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iust. R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gen <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gen Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hire <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hire Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">tyge<hi rend="italic">; am Rande:</hi> al. teah <hi rend="italic">Ld; am archaischsten</hi> teage <hi rend="italic">Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">tyge; in the margin: al. teah Ld; most archaic teage Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðisse <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðisse Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">364</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.1-5" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">desp. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">desp. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.2-4" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">n. i. <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">n. i. Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">365</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">76, 1<hi rend="italic">b fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">76, 1b lacking</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">þære</hi> und <hi rend="italic">cægean</hi> können spätwestsächs. Gen. plur. sein. Der Plural, den Lateiner annehmen, passt besser in den Zusammenhang</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">þære</hi> and <hi rend="italic">cægean</hi> may be late West Saxon gen. plur. The plural, which the Latin translators assume, fits the context better</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">weardian</hi> regiert erst Gen., dann Acc.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">weardian</hi> governs first the gen., then the acc.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">heddern</hi>: ‘<hi rend="italic">cellarium, penu</hi>’; auch <hi rend="italic">hordern</hi> (neben ‘Schatz): <hi rend="italic">cellarium</hi>, Vorratskammer’; Toller</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">heddern</hi>: ‘<hi rend="italic">cellarium, penu</hi>’; also <hi rend="italic">hordern</hi> (besides ‘treasure): <hi rend="italic">cellarium</hi>, storeroom’; Toller</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">teah</hi> in Ld ist Nom.; <hi rend="italic">tægan</hi> (B) nach -<hi rend="italic">n</hi> Decl., ist sonst nicht belegt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">teah</hi> in Ld is nom.; <hi rend="italic">tægan</hi> (B), following the -<hi rend="italic">n</hi> decl., is not otherwise attested</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Haftung 9; Brunner II 579</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Haftung 9; Brunner II 579</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The form <hi rend="italic">tægan</hi> is unusual and does not occur elsewhere, see BT. p. 972, <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi> <hi rend="italic">teah</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope></bibl><label>cæge</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">h. hordern</hi> ⁊ G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope></bibl><label>cæge</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope></bibl><label>tægan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Written in the margin in 16th cent. in B; ⁊ <hi rend="italic">hyre tege</hi> (<hi rend="italic">tyge</hi>) G, A; <hi rend="italic">tyge</hi> Ld, with in the margin <hi rend="italic">al. teah.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_76-1a.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope></bibl><label>ðone</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. cap. 25; <hi rend="italic">þonne</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
